how do i set up the disk image? I currently have the virtual machine definition in virtualbox and i have a seprate machine with the disk image

If the disk image (the Ubuntu .iso file) is currently on a completely different physical computer, you will first need to transfer that file to the host computer running VirtualBox (using a USB drive, cloud storage, or network transfer). VirtualBox needs local access to the file to boot from it.

Once the .iso file is on the same machine as your VirtualBox installation, you can attach it to your virtual machine's optical drive to begin the installation.

1
Open Storage Settings
Select your Ubuntu VM in the VirtualBox Manager and click the Settings gear icon. In the left-hand menu, click on Storage.

2
Select the Empty Drive
Under the Storage Devices tree in the middle, look for Controller: IDE (or Controller: SATA). Below it, click on the CD icon labeled Empty.

3
Attach the Disk Image
On the right side under Attributes, click the small, blue CD icon next to the "Optical Drive" dropdown. Select Choose a disk file... from the menu.

4
Select the ISO File
Navigate to the folder where you saved the Ubuntu .iso file, select it, and click Open. The word "Empty" in the storage tree should now be replaced by the name of your ISO file.

5
Save and Start
Click OK at the bottom to save your settings. Click the green Start arrow in the main VirtualBox window to power on the VM.

To verify this worked, watch the VM window as it boots. Instead of a black screen or a "no bootable medium found" error, it should load directly into the Ubuntu installation menu or setup screen.

